<ResourceDictionary xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
                    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
                    xmlns:vm="using:RimManager.App.ViewModels"
                    xmlns:mods="using:RimManager.App.Views.Mods"
                    xmlns:dm="using:RimManager.Core.Domain"
                    xmlns:ctl="using:RimManager.App.Views.Controls"
                    xmlns:sys="using:System"
                    xmlns:adc="using:Avalonia.Data.Converters">
  <!--
    Shared row DataTemplates, so the two panes and (later) the command palette all
    render a mod the same way — AVALONIA_GUIDE.md §1: "ModRowTemplates.axaml is a
    shared ResourceDictionary holding the row DataTemplates so the two panes and
    the palette can reuse them."

    Row height is {DynamicResource RmRowHeight} everywhere: one resource write
    (20 <-> 26) re-lays out every list in the app. Never a literal height, and
    never Height="Auto" — fixed rows are what make virtualization exact.

    Built against 1f: index · tag stripe · source badge · name · packageId ·
    version · one status glyph.

    The 6-slot CDPTSL content-flags column was REMOVED in N1 (NEXT_PLAN §0a). Six
    letters of jargon in the densest part of the window is not readable at a glance
    even once you know the key. The facts are real and were NOT deleted with it: mod
    info spells them out as words ("C# code · XML patches · Textures"), which is where
    you are standing when you care, and ContentFlags in Core is untouched.
  -->

  <!-- ========================== source badge ============================= -->
  <!--
    N1 · the SRC column is an icon per source, not a letter (design non-negotiable
    #12 wants real geometries wherever a mark is drawn). Defined ONCE and used by both
    row templates AND mod info's source pill: this is six visibility bindings and six
    geometries, and the status slot below shows what happens when a block like this
    gets written out twice — the two copies are only identical until someone edits one.

    Typed to IModSourceBadge rather than to a view model, which is what lets mod info
    share it: ModRowViewModel and ModDetailViewModel both implement it. Mod info drew
    a LETTER ("D · DLC") until the interface existed, so one source had two marks.

    Six PathIcons in a Panel, exactly as the status slot picks among its four, rather
    than a converter or a geometry-valued view-model property: a converter hands back a
    value frozen at conversion time, and a geometry property would drag Avalonia
    resources into a view model that is deliberately Avalonia-free.

    Nothing here sets Foreground locally. The tint is a style setter keyed off the
    same bound class as the background (Controls.axaml, Border.srcBadge.srcX PathIcon)
    — a local value on the element would outrank it, which is the single trap that has
    cost this project three shipped bugs.
  -->
  <DataTemplate x:Key="SourceBadgeTemplate" x:DataType="vm:IModSourceBadge">
    <Border Classes="srcBadge"
            Classes.srcCore="{Binding IsCoreSource}"
            Classes.srcDlc="{Binding IsDlcSource}"
            Classes.srcWorkshop="{Binding IsWorkshopSource}"
            Classes.srcLocal="{Binding IsLocalSource}"
            Classes.srcGit="{Binding IsGitSource}"
            ToolTip.Tip="{Binding Source}">
      <Panel>
        <PathIcon Data="{StaticResource RmIconSourceCore}" Width="9" Height="9"
                  IsVisible="{Binding IsCoreSource}" />
        <PathIcon Data="{StaticResource RmIconSourceDlc}" Width="9" Height="9"
                  IsVisible="{Binding IsDlcSource}" />
        <PathIcon Data="{StaticResource RmIconSourceWorkshop}" Width="9" Height="9"
                  IsVisible="{Binding IsWorkshopSource}" />
        <PathIcon Data="{StaticResource RmIconSourceLocal}" Width="9" Height="9"
                  IsVisible="{Binding IsLocalSource}" />
        <PathIcon Data="{StaticResource RmIconGitBranch}" Width="9" Height="9"
                  IsVisible="{Binding IsGitSource}" />
      </Panel>
    </Border>
  </DataTemplate>

  <!-- ======================= mod row (active pane) ======================= -->
  <!--
    Columns are the 1f compact set, 8px horizontal padding:
      index 28 · stripe 3 · badge 14 · name * · packageId 150 · ver 52 · status 16
    Fixed widths on every column but the name are what let the eye compare
    vertically down a 200-row list. The 53px the flags column gave up goes to NAME,
    which is the column that was short of room.
  -->
  <DataTemplate x:Key="ModRowTemplate" x:DataType="vm:ModRowViewModel">
    <!-- Drag state rides bound classes on this Border (dim to 35% while dragging,
         accent tint for 1.2s after a drop). Bound classes work on an element;
         Style setters named "Classes.x" do not.

         conflictLoss / conflictWin are N6's selection-relative highlights: while a
         mod is selected, red = the selected mod wins against this row, green = this
         row wins against it. -->
    <Border Classes="row" Classes.dragSource="{Binding IsDragSource}"
            Classes.justMoved="{Binding IsJustMoved}"
            Classes.conflictLoss="{Binding IsOverwrittenBySelected}"
            Classes.conflictWin="{Binding OverwritesSelected}"
            Classes.harmonyShared="{Binding SharesHarmonyWithSelected}">
    <!-- The relationship paints carry a RIGHT-edge second channel (v2 §4A.2):
         solid ok/bad for win/lose, DASHED harmony for shares-a-target — dashed
         because the relationship is linked-not-ranked and names no winner. A Line
         because an Avalonia Border cannot dash; the Panel clips its overshoot.

         The Panel's Height is LOAD-BEARING: the Line measures at its geometry's
         64px, and ClipToBounds clips paint, not measure — without the fixed
         height, every harmony-sharing row ballooned to 64px the moment a mod
         with shared targets was selected. -->
    <Panel ClipToBounds="True" Height="{DynamicResource RmRowHeight}">
    <Rectangle Width="2" HorizontalAlignment="Right"
               Fill="{DynamicResource RmSuccessBrush}"
               IsVisible="{Binding OverwritesSelected}" />
    <Rectangle Width="2" HorizontalAlignment="Right"
               Fill="{DynamicResource RmDangerBrush}"
               IsVisible="{Binding IsOverwrittenBySelected}" />
    <Line StartPoint="1,0" EndPoint="1,64" Width="2" HorizontalAlignment="Right"
          Stroke="{DynamicResource RmHarmonyBrush}" StrokeThickness="2"
          StrokeDashArray="1.5,1.5"
          IsVisible="{Binding SharesHarmonyWithSelected}" />
    <!--
      28,7,14,7,*,7,150,7,52,7,20,7,16 at every width except below 900 (2k),
      where packageId and version collapse to zero and a `›` appears instead. The
      active list's columns are FIXED — it is the load order, not a table (#3) — so
      this is not a picker; it is the one width the breakpoint takes away.

      The 3px tag stripe column is GONE (v2 §4A.1): tags ride the pill zone inside
      the NAME cell now, every tag represented.

      Column 10 is the ⚡ conflict badge (N6) — its own slot, NOT the status slot:
      a conflict is not a warning and a row can carry both at once. 20px because it
      holds the bolt AND the direction mark beside it. Active rows only; the
      inactive template has no such column because an unloaded mod overrides nothing.
    -->
    <Grid Height="{DynamicResource RmRowHeight}" Margin="8,0">
      <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
        <ColumnDefinition Width="28" />
        <ColumnDefinition Width="7" />
        <ColumnDefinition Width="14" />
        <ColumnDefinition Width="7" />
        <ColumnDefinition Width="*" />
        <ColumnDefinition Width="7" />
        <ColumnDefinition Width="{Binding $parent[Window].((vm:MainWindowViewModel)DataContext).RowPackageIdWidth}" />
        <ColumnDefinition Width="7" />
        <ColumnDefinition Width="{Binding $parent[Window].((vm:MainWindowViewModel)DataContext).RowVersionWidth}" />
        <ColumnDefinition Width="7" />
        <ColumnDefinition Width="20" />
        <ColumnDefinition Width="7" />
        <ColumnDefinition Width="16" />
        <ColumnDefinition Width="{Binding $parent[Window].((vm:MainWindowViewModel)DataContext).RowChevronWidth}" />
      </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>


      <!-- The "who wins" number. Renumbers live during a drag. -->
      <TextBlock Grid.Column="0" Text="{Binding Index}" Classes="idx" />

      <!-- Icon AND tint, never tint alone; the tooltip names the source in words. -->
      <ContentControl Grid.Column="2" Content="{Binding}"
                      ContentTemplate="{StaticResource SourceBadgeTemplate}"
                      VerticalAlignment="Center" />

      <!-- NAME plus the tag-pill zone (v2 §4A.1). The zone's budget is WHAT IS LEFT
           after the name keeps its 110px minimum — not a fixed cap. A flat
           MaxWidth="132" made the degradation ladder fire on free space: a short
           name on a wide window collapsed to dots and "+2" with half the row empty,
           because the cap cannot see the row. Pills are INERT here — editing stays
           at Mod Info's chips — and the tooltip lists every tag. -->
      <mods:NamePillPanel Grid.Column="4">
        <!-- Core, DLC and pinned mods render at 600: they anchor the order. -->
        <TextBlock Text="{Binding Name}" Classes="pri" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                   TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis" ToolTip.Tip="{Binding Name}"
                   Classes.anchor="{Binding IsAnchor}" />
        <mods:TagPillStrip Margin="6,0,0,0" VerticalAlignment="Stretch"
                           Pills="{Binding Pills}" ToolTip.Tip="{Binding TagTip}"
                           IsVisible="{Binding $parent[Window].((vm:MainWindowViewModel)DataContext).ShowTagStripes}" />
      </mods:NamePillPanel>

      <TextBlock Grid.Column="6" Text="{Binding PackageIdText}" Classes="mono ter"
                 VerticalAlignment="Center" TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis"
                 ToolTip.Tip="{Binding PackageIdText}" />

      <!-- For the 1.2s after a drop this column shows "was 114" instead of the
           version, so the move can be confirmed without hunting for the row again
           (3a §4). -->
      <TextBlock Grid.Column="8" Text="{Binding Version}" Classes="mono ter"
                 VerticalAlignment="Center" TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis"
                 IsVisible="{Binding !IsJustMoved}" />
      <TextBlock Grid.Column="8" Text="{Binding PreviousIndexText}" Classes="mono"
                 Foreground="{DynamicResource RmAccentTextBrush}"
                 VerticalAlignment="Center" IsVisible="{Binding IsJustMoved}" />

      <!-- The conflict badge (N6, §0f, owner's two-channel system): the MARK beside
           the bolt carries the override story — + this row's contested content
           survives (green), − it is discarded (red), both as a green + stacked over
           a red −, each half keeping its singular colour. The BOLT's colour carries
           the harmony bit: yellow = overrides only, blue = harmony is involved (the
           mark says whether overrides are too), no bolt = no conflict at all.
           Win/lose grammar never touches harmony — every patch runs (§0f).

           A Button, because clicking it opens the per-mod conflict window (N6b).
           IsHitTestVisible, not IsEnabled, for the status slot's reason: a disabled
           Fluent button dims its content. -->
      <Button Grid.Column="10" Classes="affordance" Padding="0"
              VerticalAlignment="Stretch" HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
              IsHitTestVisible="{Binding HasConflicts}"
              Command="{Binding $parent[Window].((vm:MainWindowViewModel)DataContext).OpenModConflictsCommand}"
              CommandParameter="{Binding}"
              ToolTip.Tip="{Binding ConflictTip}"
              AutomationProperties.Name="Show this mod's conflicts">
        <Grid ColumnDefinitions="10,2,6" VerticalAlignment="Center" HorizontalAlignment="Center"
              IsVisible="{Binding HasConflicts}">
          <Panel Grid.Column="0" VerticalAlignment="Center">
            <PathIcon Data="{StaticResource RmIconConflict}" Width="10" Height="10"
                      Foreground="{DynamicResource RmWarningBrush}"
                      IsVisible="{Binding IsOverrideOnlyConflict}" />
            <!-- RmHarmonyBrush, not accent (UI audit): the legend one column over
                 teaches BLUE bolt = Harmony involved, and under Drop Pods the accent
                 is amber - the row was contradicting its own legend. -->
            <PathIcon Data="{StaticResource RmIconConflict}" Width="10" Height="10"
                      Foreground="{DynamicResource RmHarmonyBrush}"
                      IsVisible="{Binding HasHarmonyConflict}" />
          </Panel>
          <Panel Grid.Column="2" VerticalAlignment="Center">
            <PathIcon Data="{StaticResource RmIconOverwriting}" Width="6" Height="6"
                      Foreground="{DynamicResource RmSuccessBrush}"
                      IsVisible="{Binding IsOverwritingOnly}" />
            <PathIcon Data="{StaticResource RmIconOverwritten}" Width="6" Height="6"
                      Foreground="{DynamicResource RmDangerBrush}"
                      IsVisible="{Binding IsOverwrittenOnly}" />
            <StackPanel IsVisible="{Binding IsMixedConflict}" Spacing="1"
                        VerticalAlignment="Center">
              <PathIcon Data="{StaticResource RmIconOverwriting}" Width="5" Height="5"
                        Foreground="{DynamicResource RmSuccessBrush}" />
              <PathIcon Data="{StaticResource RmIconOverwritten}" Width="5" Height="5"
                        Foreground="{DynamicResource RmDangerBrush}" />
            </StackPanel>
          </Panel>
        </Grid>
      </Button>

      <!-- ONE status slot, strict precedence: broken -> warning -> update -> git
           dirty -> blank. A row never shows two. Each carries a tooltip, because
           colour is never the only signal — and since N2 that tooltip NAMES the
           warnings rather than announcing that some exist, which is what the coloured
           mark beside it already said.

           A Button, because clicking it opens the Warnings dock on the warning it
           stands for (UI-4). Hit-testing is off when nothing in that dock names the
           mod: this glyph is also raised for an update and for a dirty working tree,
           and a click landing on a tab that does not mention your mod is worse than a
           click that does nothing.

           IsHitTestVisible rather than IsEnabled, because a disabled Fluent button
           dims its content — which would render the most urgent rows the faintest.
           Padding 0 so the 11px glyph stays centred in the 16px column the header
           legends; Button.affordance's own 4,0 would shift it off. -->
      <Button Grid.Column="12" Classes="affordance" Padding="0"
              VerticalAlignment="Stretch" HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
              IsHitTestVisible="{Binding HasWarnings}"
              Command="{Binding $parent[Window].((vm:MainWindowViewModel)DataContext).RevealWarningsForCommand}"
              CommandParameter="{Binding}"
              ToolTip.Tip="{Binding StatusTip}"
              AutomationProperties.Name="Show this mod's warnings">
        <Panel>
          <PathIcon Data="{StaticResource RmIconError}" Width="11" Height="11"
                    Foreground="{DynamicResource RmDangerBrush}" IsVisible="{Binding IsBroken}" />
          <PathIcon Data="{StaticResource RmIconWarning}" Width="11" Height="11"
                    Foreground="{DynamicResource RmWarningBrush}" IsVisible="{Binding IsWarning}" />
          <PathIcon Data="{StaticResource RmIconUpdate}" Width="11" Height="11"
                    Foreground="{DynamicResource RmAccentBrush}" IsVisible="{Binding HasUpdate}" />
          <PathIcon Data="{StaticResource RmIconGitBranch}" Width="11" Height="11"
                    Foreground="{DynamicResource RmAccentBrush}" IsVisible="{Binding IsGitDirty}" />
        </Panel>
      </Button>

      <!--
        2k · the `›` that opens the info sheet whenever mod info is an overlay — both
        breakpoints, not only the segmented one. Its COLUMN is what appears and
        disappears, so the button needs no IsVisible of its own, and must not have one:
        a local value would outrank any style trying to manage it.

        Always rendered at text.tertiary and only brightened, never hover-revealed
        (#11): on a 20px row a chevron that appears under the pointer is unfindable.
      -->
      <Button Grid.Column="13" Classes="affordance" Padding="0"
              VerticalAlignment="Stretch" HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
              Command="{Binding $parent[Window].((vm:MainWindowViewModel)DataContext).OpenInfoDrawerCommand}"
              AutomationProperties.Name="Show details for this mod">
        <PathIcon Data="{StaticResource RmIconChevronRight}" Width="9" Height="9" />
      </Button>
    </Grid>
    </Panel>
    </Border>
  </DataTemplate>

  <!-- ============== mod row, narrow (inactive pane: no index) ============= -->
  <!-- An inactive mod has no position, so it gets no index column (1a). -->
  <DataTemplate x:Key="InactiveModRowTemplate" x:DataType="vm:ModRowViewModel">
    <Border Classes="row" Classes.dragSource="{Binding IsDragSource}"
            Classes.justMoved="{Binding IsJustMoved}">
    <!--
      N1 · these widths come from the PANE's measured width, not from Columns ▾ (which
      is gone) and not from the window's. The splitter is user-draggable, so the window
      says nothing about how much room this list has; widening the pane reveals VER,
      then AUTHOR, then PACKAGEID, cheapest first, and never below a 150px NAME.

      Column-for-column identical to the header above the list — the guard in
      AdaptiveLayoutMarkupTests pins that, because a legend one column out of step with
      its data is invisible until you read a value against the wrong heading.

      A hidden column collapses to zero rather than merely blanking its content, or
      "gone" would read as "empty". The ACTIVE list is not configurable at all: it is
      the load order, not a table (#3).
    -->
    <Grid Height="{DynamicResource RmRowHeight}" Margin="8,0">
      <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
        <ColumnDefinition Width="{Binding $parent[Window].((vm:MainWindowViewModel)DataContext).SourceColumnWidth}" />
        <ColumnDefinition Width="7" />
        <ColumnDefinition Width="*" />
        <ColumnDefinition Width="7" />
        <ColumnDefinition Width="{Binding $parent[Window].((vm:MainWindowViewModel)DataContext).PackageIdColumnWidth}" />
        <ColumnDefinition Width="7" />
        <ColumnDefinition Width="{Binding $parent[Window].((vm:MainWindowViewModel)DataContext).AuthorColumnWidth}" />
        <ColumnDefinition Width="7" />
        <ColumnDefinition Width="{Binding $parent[Window].((vm:MainWindowViewModel)DataContext).VersionColumnWidth}" />
        <ColumnDefinition Width="7" />
        <ColumnDefinition Width="16" />
        <ColumnDefinition Width="{Binding $parent[Window].((vm:MainWindowViewModel)DataContext).RowChevronWidth}" />
      </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
      <ContentControl Grid.Column="0" Content="{Binding}"
                      ContentTemplate="{StaticResource SourceBadgeTemplate}"
                      VerticalAlignment="Center" />
      <!-- NAME plus the pill zone, the active row's grammar (v2 §4A.1) — the 3px
           stripe column is gone here too. -->
      <mods:NamePillPanel Grid.Column="2">
        <TextBlock Text="{Binding Name}" Classes="pri" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                   TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis" ToolTip.Tip="{Binding Name}"
                   Classes.anchor="{Binding IsAnchor}" />
        <mods:TagPillStrip Margin="6,0,0,0" VerticalAlignment="Stretch"
                           Pills="{Binding Pills}" ToolTip.Tip="{Binding TagTip}"
                           IsVisible="{Binding $parent[Window].((vm:MainWindowViewModel)DataContext).ShowTagStripes}" />
      </mods:NamePillPanel>
      <TextBlock Grid.Column="4" Text="{Binding PackageIdText}" Classes="mono ter"
                 VerticalAlignment="Center" TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis"
                 ToolTip.Tip="{Binding PackageIdText}" />
      <TextBlock Grid.Column="6" Text="{Binding Author}" Classes="small ter"
                 VerticalAlignment="Center" TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis"
                 ToolTip.Tip="{Binding Author}" />
      <TextBlock Grid.Column="8" Text="{Binding Version}" Classes="mono ter"
                 VerticalAlignment="Center" TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis" />
      <Button Grid.Column="10" Classes="affordance" Padding="0"
              VerticalAlignment="Stretch" HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
              IsHitTestVisible="{Binding HasWarnings}"
              Command="{Binding $parent[Window].((vm:MainWindowViewModel)DataContext).RevealWarningsForCommand}"
              CommandParameter="{Binding}"
              ToolTip.Tip="{Binding StatusTip}"
              AutomationProperties.Name="Show this mod's warnings">
        <Panel>
          <PathIcon Data="{StaticResource RmIconError}" Width="11" Height="11"
                    Foreground="{DynamicResource RmDangerBrush}" IsVisible="{Binding IsBroken}" />
          <PathIcon Data="{StaticResource RmIconWarning}" Width="11" Height="11"
                    Foreground="{DynamicResource RmWarningBrush}" IsVisible="{Binding IsWarning}" />
          <PathIcon Data="{StaticResource RmIconUpdate}" Width="11" Height="11"
                    Foreground="{DynamicResource RmAccentBrush}" IsVisible="{Binding HasUpdate}" />
          <PathIcon Data="{StaticResource RmIconGitBranch}" Width="11" Height="11"
                    Foreground="{DynamicResource RmAccentBrush}" IsVisible="{Binding IsGitDirty}" />
        </Panel>
      </Button>

      <!-- 2k · the same `›` as the active row; its COLUMN is what appears. -->
      <Button Grid.Column="12" Classes="affordance" Padding="0"
              VerticalAlignment="Stretch" HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
              Command="{Binding $parent[Window].((vm:MainWindowViewModel)DataContext).OpenInfoDrawerCommand}"
              AutomationProperties.Name="Show details for this mod">
        <PathIcon Data="{StaticResource RmIconChevronRight}" Width="9" Height="9" />
      </Button>
    </Grid>
    </Border>
  </DataTemplate>

  <!-- ============================= separator ============================= -->
  <!--
    Always 22px regardless of density (1f). The 4px colour bar is full-bleed, floor
    to ceiling — the only place a separator colour goes edge to edge, and what makes
    group boundaries readable while scrolling fast.
  -->
  <DataTemplate x:Key="SeparatorRowTemplate" x:DataType="vm:SeparatorRowViewModel">
    <Border Classes="separatorRow">
      <!-- Right-click and the ⋮ button carry the SAME five items. Written out twice
           because a MenuFlyout cannot be shared between two parents and this project
           has already been bitten by a data-driven menu setting Header as a local
           value. SeparatorMenuTests compares the two blocks, so the copy that gets
           edited alone fails the build rather than drifting quietly - which is how
           Apply-and-launch ended up live in one place and dead in another. -->
      <Border.ContextMenu>
        <ContextMenu>
          <MenuItem Header="Rename" InputGesture="F2" Command="{Binding BeginRenameCommand}" />
          <!-- Rows are in Palette's own index order, and each parameter IS that index.
               They used to read Blue Green Violet Amber Red Slate against 0..5, so
               three of six painted the wrong hue: Violet gave amber, Amber gave red,
               Red gave violet. SeparatorMenuTests compared the two copies only to each
               other, so both being wrong agreed perfectly — SeparatorColourTests now
               pins each label against Palette. -->
          <MenuItem Header="Colour">
            <MenuItem Header="Blue" Command="{Binding ChooseColorCommand}">
              <MenuItem.CommandParameter><sys:Int32>0</sys:Int32></MenuItem.CommandParameter>
            </MenuItem>
            <MenuItem Header="Green" Command="{Binding ChooseColorCommand}">
              <MenuItem.CommandParameter><sys:Int32>1</sys:Int32></MenuItem.CommandParameter>
            </MenuItem>
            <MenuItem Header="Amber" Command="{Binding ChooseColorCommand}">
              <MenuItem.CommandParameter><sys:Int32>2</sys:Int32></MenuItem.CommandParameter>
            </MenuItem>
            <MenuItem Header="Red" Command="{Binding ChooseColorCommand}">
              <MenuItem.CommandParameter><sys:Int32>3</sys:Int32></MenuItem.CommandParameter>
            </MenuItem>
            <MenuItem Header="Violet" Command="{Binding ChooseColorCommand}">
              <MenuItem.CommandParameter><sys:Int32>4</sys:Int32></MenuItem.CommandParameter>
            </MenuItem>
            <MenuItem Header="Slate" Command="{Binding ChooseColorCommand}">
              <MenuItem.CommandParameter><sys:Int32>5</sys:Int32></MenuItem.CommandParameter>
            </MenuItem>
          </MenuItem>
          <MenuItem Header="{Binding CollapseMenuLabel}" Command="{Binding ToggleCollapseCommand}" />
          <Separator />
          <MenuItem Header="Delete separator" Command="{Binding DeleteCommand}"
                    ToolTip.Tip="Removes the header. The mods under it stay exactly where they are." />
        </ContextMenu>
      </Border.ContextMenu>
      <!-- Column 5 is the ✓ that commits a rename. Auto, so it costs nothing at all
           when the row is not being edited. -->
      <Grid ColumnDefinitions="4,8,12,6,Auto,Auto,8,Auto,10,*,Auto">

        <Border Grid.Column="0" Classes="paletted"
                Classes.p0="{Binding IsPalette0}" Classes.p1="{Binding IsPalette1}"
                Classes.p2="{Binding IsPalette2}" Classes.p3="{Binding IsPalette3}"
                Classes.p4="{Binding IsPalette4}" Classes.p5="{Binding IsPalette5}" />

        <Button Grid.Column="2" Command="{Binding ToggleCollapseCommand}" Classes="affordance"
                Padding="0" VerticalAlignment="Center" AutomationProperties.Name="Collapse group">
          <PathIcon Width="9" Height="9"
                    Data="{StaticResource RmIconChevronDown}"
                    IsVisible="{Binding !Collapsed}" />
        </Button>
        <Button Grid.Column="2" Command="{Binding ToggleCollapseCommand}" Classes="affordance"
                Padding="0" VerticalAlignment="Center" IsVisible="{Binding Collapsed}"
                AutomationProperties.Name="Expand group">
          <PathIcon Data="{StaticResource RmIconChevronRight}" Width="9" Height="9" />
        </Button>

        <!-- 10px/700 upper-case, tinted with the separator's own colour (1f).
             Displayed as a TextBlock and only swapped for a TextBox while renaming:
             a TextBox cannot render caps without fighting the user's typing, and its
             taller line box sits the text lower than the chevron and count beside
             it, which reads as a misaligned row. -->
        <TextBlock Grid.Column="4" Text="{Binding DisplayName}" Classes="separatorLabel palettedText"
                   IsVisible="{Binding IsNotEditing}"
                   Classes.p0="{Binding IsPalette0}" Classes.p1="{Binding IsPalette1}"
                   Classes.p2="{Binding IsPalette2}" Classes.p3="{Binding IsPalette3}"
                   Classes.p4="{Binding IsPalette4}" Classes.p5="{Binding IsPalette5}" />
        <TextBox Grid.Column="4" AutomationProperties.Name="Separator name"
                 ctl:EditFocus.FocusOnShow="True"
                 Text="{Binding Name, Mode=TwoWay}" BorderThickness="0"
                 Background="Transparent" Padding="0" MinWidth="80" MinHeight="0"
                 VerticalAlignment="Center" VerticalContentAlignment="Center"
                 FontWeight="Bold" FontSize="{DynamicResource RmFontSizeMono}"
                 IsVisible="{Binding IsEditing}" PlaceholderText="SEPARATOR">
          <TextBox.KeyBindings>
            <KeyBinding Gesture="Enter" Command="{Binding EndRenameCommand}" />
            <!-- Escape RESTORES. It used to run EndRename, so the key that means
                 "abandon this" committed it instead - the name binding pushes on
                 every keystroke, so by the time Escape arrived there was nothing
                 left to abandon. -->
            <KeyBinding Gesture="Escape" Command="{Binding CancelRenameCommand}" />
          </TextBox.KeyBindings>
        </TextBox>

        <!-- The edit affordance: a 1px rule under the field in the separator's own
             colour. Reuses Border.paletted, which sets Background - a 1px border
             filled with the hue IS the underline, so this needs no new style.
             Without it the box was transparent and borderless, and nothing on the
             row said it had become editable. -->
        <Border Grid.Column="4" Height="1" VerticalAlignment="Bottom" Margin="0,0,0,2"
                IsVisible="{Binding IsEditing}" Classes="paletted"
                Classes.p0="{Binding IsPalette0}" Classes.p1="{Binding IsPalette1}"
                Classes.p2="{Binding IsPalette2}" Classes.p3="{Binding IsPalette3}"
                Classes.p4="{Binding IsPalette4}" Classes.p5="{Binding IsPalette5}" />

        <!-- Commit. Enter does it too, but a key nobody is told about is not an
             affordance - and the check is tinted with the separator's own colour, so
             the control that ends the edit is visibly part of the thing being edited. -->
        <Button Grid.Column="5" Classes="affordance" Padding="4,0" Margin="6,0,0,0"
                VerticalAlignment="Stretch" IsVisible="{Binding IsEditing}"
                Command="{Binding EndRenameCommand}"
                AutomationProperties.Name="Save separator name"
                ToolTip.Tip="Save this name — Enter. Escape restores the old one.">
          <PathIcon Data="{StaticResource RmIconCheck}" Width="10" Height="10"
                    Classes="palettedText"
                    Classes.p0="{Binding IsPalette0}" Classes.p1="{Binding IsPalette1}"
                    Classes.p2="{Binding IsPalette2}" Classes.p3="{Binding IsPalette3}"
                    Classes.p4="{Binding IsPalette4}" Classes.p5="{Binding IsPalette5}" />
        </Button>

        <!-- The count is ALWAYS shown, so a collapsed group still reports its size. -->
        <TextBlock Grid.Column="7" Classes="micro" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                   Text="{Binding CountText}" />

        <!-- A 1px rule fills the remaining width, then the ⋮ menu. -->
        <Border Grid.Column="9" Height="1" VerticalAlignment="Center" Classes="divider" />

        <Button Grid.Column="10" Classes="affordance" Padding="6,0" VerticalAlignment="Stretch"
                AutomationProperties.Name="Group menu">
          <PathIcon Data="{StaticResource RmIconKebab}" Width="11" Height="11" />
          <Button.Flyout>
            <MenuFlyout>
              <MenuItem Header="Rename" InputGesture="F2" Command="{Binding BeginRenameCommand}" />
              <MenuItem Header="Colour">
                <MenuItem Header="Blue" Command="{Binding ChooseColorCommand}">
                  <MenuItem.CommandParameter><sys:Int32>0</sys:Int32></MenuItem.CommandParameter>
                </MenuItem>
                <MenuItem Header="Green" Command="{Binding ChooseColorCommand}">
                  <MenuItem.CommandParameter><sys:Int32>1</sys:Int32></MenuItem.CommandParameter>
                </MenuItem>
                <MenuItem Header="Amber" Command="{Binding ChooseColorCommand}">
                  <MenuItem.CommandParameter><sys:Int32>2</sys:Int32></MenuItem.CommandParameter>
                </MenuItem>
                <MenuItem Header="Red" Command="{Binding ChooseColorCommand}">
                  <MenuItem.CommandParameter><sys:Int32>3</sys:Int32></MenuItem.CommandParameter>
                </MenuItem>
                <MenuItem Header="Violet" Command="{Binding ChooseColorCommand}">
                  <MenuItem.CommandParameter><sys:Int32>4</sys:Int32></MenuItem.CommandParameter>
                </MenuItem>
                <MenuItem Header="Slate" Command="{Binding ChooseColorCommand}">
                  <MenuItem.CommandParameter><sys:Int32>5</sys:Int32></MenuItem.CommandParameter>
                </MenuItem>
              </MenuItem>
              <MenuItem Header="{Binding CollapseMenuLabel}" Command="{Binding ToggleCollapseCommand}" />
              <Separator />
              <MenuItem Header="Delete separator" Command="{Binding DeleteCommand}"
                        ToolTip.Tip="Removes the header. The mods under it stay exactly where they are." />
            </MenuFlyout>
          </Button.Flyout>
        </Button>
      </Grid>
    </Border>
  </DataTemplate>

  <!-- =========================== mod info body =========================== -->
  <!--
    1a §2-9, in this FIXED order: preview · identity · tag chips · facts grid ·
    dependencies · notes · description · actions. Fixed because the pane is read
    while reordering — the eye needs the same thing in the same place every time,
    not a layout that reflows with whatever data happens to exist.
  -->
  <DataTemplate x:Key="ModDetailTemplate" DataType="vm:ModDetailViewModel">
    <ScrollViewer>
      <StackPanel>

        <!-- 2 · preview, FIT into a 344x160 band (O21). COLLAPSES TO ZERO when the mod
             has none — no grey placeholder box. -->
        <!-- Two nested conditions rather than one converter: the preference collapses
             the slot entirely, and within it "no preview" collapses it too — the
             design is explicit that this goes to zero height, never to a grey box. -->
        <!-- Uniform, not UniformToFill: the whole image is shown rather than an
             excerpt of it. It used to crop, and since 540 of 546 real previews are
             TALLER than this band, cropping is what most of them got — the art was
             sliced through the middle. Fitting letterboxes instead, onto the pane's own
             background, which costs some empty space on a square preview and shows the
             author's actual artwork on every one.
             Still a BUTTON (N8): full size is a click away, and the tooltip carries the
             real pixel dimensions. Nothing hover-revealed (#11), and hover changes
             nothing: an opaque image leaves a hover background nowhere to show. -->
        <Border IsVisible="{Binding $parent[Window].((vm:MainWindowViewModel)DataContext).ShowPreviewImages}">
        <Button Classes="previewImage" Height="{DynamicResource RmModInfoPreviewHeight}"
                IsVisible="{Binding HasPreview}"
                Command="{Binding $parent[Window].((vm:MainWindowViewModel)DataContext).OpenPreviewImageCommand}"
                ToolTip.Tip="{Binding PreviewTooltip}"
                AutomationProperties.Name="View the full preview image">
          <Image Source="{Binding Preview}" Stretch="Uniform" />
        </Button>
        </Border>

        <!-- 3 · identity -->
        <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto" Margin="10,10,10,0">
          <StackPanel Grid.Column="0" Spacing="2">
            <TextBlock Text="{Binding Name}" Classes="title" TextWrapping="Wrap" />
            <TextBlock Text="{Binding PackageId}" Classes="mono ter"
                       TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis" ToolTip.Tip="{Binding PackageId}" />
          </StackPanel>
          <!-- 1a §3 draws this as mark + word. The mark is now the SAME badge the list
               rows carry — it used to be a letter, so one source had two spellings and
               nothing tied the "D" in here to the icon out there. -->
          <Border Grid.Column="1" Height="18" CornerRadius="9" Padding="5,0,8,0" Margin="8,0,0,0"
                  VerticalAlignment="Top" Background="{DynamicResource RmBackgroundAltBrush}">
            <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="5" VerticalAlignment="Center">
              <ContentControl Content="{Binding}"
                              ContentTemplate="{StaticResource SourceBadgeTemplate}"
                              VerticalAlignment="Center" />
              <TextBlock Text="{Binding SourceLabel}" Classes="mono ter" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
            </StackPanel>
          </Border>
        </Grid>

        <!-- 4 · tags. The full chips live HERE (1e §4): the rows carry the
             compact pill zone (v2 §4A.1 — the 3px stripe is retired), and these
             named chips are what stop row colour being the sole carrier of
             meaning. -->
        <StackPanel Margin="10,10,10,0" Spacing="4">
          <TextBlock Text="TAGS" Classes="micro" />
          <WrapPanel Orientation="Horizontal">
            <!-- O14 · favourite, as a pill in the same row as the tags. It leads them
                 because it is the mod's own mark rather than one of a set, and it is
                 present only when set — an empty favourite pill would be a control,
                 and the header star is already the control. Clicking clears it, which
                 is the × grammar the tag chips beside it use. -->
            <Border Classes="favPill" Margin="0,0,4,4"
                    IsVisible="{Binding Favorite}">
              <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="5">
                <PathIcon Data="{StaticResource RmIconFavorite}" Width="8" Height="8"
                          VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                <TextBlock Text="Favourite" Classes="small" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                <Button Classes="affordance" Padding="1,0"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Remove from favourites"
                        Command="{Binding $parent[Window].((vm:MainWindowViewModel)DataContext).ClearFavouriteCommand}">
                  <PathIcon Data="{StaticResource RmIconClose}" Width="7" Height="7" />
                </Button>
              </StackPanel>
            </Border>

            <ItemsControl ItemsSource="{Binding $parent[Window].((vm:MainWindowViewModel)DataContext).SelectedModTags}">
              <ItemsControl.ItemsPanel>
                <ItemsPanelTemplate>
                  <WrapPanel Orientation="Horizontal" />
                </ItemsPanelTemplate>
              </ItemsControl.ItemsPanel>
              <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                <DataTemplate x:DataType="vm:TagChipViewModel">
                  <Border Classes="card" Padding="6,1" Margin="0,0,4,4" CornerRadius="3">
                    <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="5">
                      <Border Width="8" Height="8" CornerRadius="4" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                              Classes="paletted"
                              Classes.p0="{Binding IsPalette0}" Classes.p1="{Binding IsPalette1}"
                              Classes.p2="{Binding IsPalette2}" Classes.p3="{Binding IsPalette3}"
                              Classes.p4="{Binding IsPalette4}" Classes.p5="{Binding IsPalette5}" />
                      <TextBlock Text="{Binding Name}" Classes="small sec" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                      <!-- Always rendered at text.tertiary and only brightened, never
                           hover-revealed (#11). -->
                      <Button Classes="affordance" Padding="1,0"
                              AutomationProperties.Name="Remove this tag"
                              Command="{Binding $parent[Window].((vm:MainWindowViewModel)DataContext).ToggleTagCommand}"
                              CommandParameter="{Binding Id}">
                        <PathIcon Data="{StaticResource RmIconClose}" Width="7" Height="7" />
                      </Button>
                    </StackPanel>
                  </Border>
                </DataTemplate>
              </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
            </ItemsControl>

            <!-- + Tag: assign an existing tag, or type a name to create one. Creating
                 from here keeps tagging inside the keyboard loop (1e §2). -->
            <Button Classes="quiet" Height="20" Padding="6,0" Margin="0,0,4,4">
              <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="4">
                <PathIcon Data="{StaticResource RmIconPlus}" Width="8" Height="8"
                          VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                <TextBlock Text="Tag" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
              </StackPanel>
              <Button.Flyout>
                <!--
                  O7/O8 · the assign flyout, on the same grammar as the Tags ▾ filter:
                  no checkboxes, a tick in a fixed 14px slot, search, and a bounded
                  scroll. It acts on the SELECTION, not on the one mod whose info pane
                  it hangs off — which is why the heading counts. Every tag is listed,
                  assigned or not, because a tri-state needs the assigned ones present
                  to show "1 of 3"; the old flyout listed only the unassigned.
                -->
                <Flyout Placement="BottomEdgeAlignedLeft">
                  <StackPanel Width="250" Spacing="1">
                    <TextBlock Margin="8,6,8,4" Classes="micro"
                               Text="{Binding $parent[Window].((vm:MainWindowViewModel)DataContext).AssignHeading}" />

                    <TextBox Margin="6,0,6,2" AutomationProperties.Name="Search tags"
                             Text="{Binding $parent[Window].((vm:MainWindowViewModel)DataContext).AssignSearch, Mode=TwoWay}"
                             PlaceholderText="Search tags…" />

                    <!-- Both lines point at Settings now that the create box has gone (O22).
                         A dead end that names no way forward is the thing the empty-state
                         pass (3e) exists to prevent. -->
                    <TextBlock Margin="8,4" Classes="small ter" TextWrapping="Wrap"
                               IsVisible="{Binding $parent[Window].((vm:MainWindowViewModel)DataContext).AssignSearchFoundNothing}"
                               Text="No tag matches that. New tags are made in Settings ▸ Tags." />

                    <TextBlock Margin="8,4" Classes="small ter" TextWrapping="Wrap"
                               IsVisible="{Binding $parent[Window].((vm:MainWindowViewModel)DataContext).HasNoTagsAtAll}"
                               Text="No tags yet. Make the first one in Settings ▸ Tags." />

                    <ScrollViewer MaxHeight="260" VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto">
                      <ItemsControl ItemsSource="{Binding $parent[Window].((vm:MainWindowViewModel)DataContext).VisibleAssignRows}">
                        <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                          <DataTemplate x:DataType="vm:TagAssignRowViewModel">
                            <Button Classes="listRow" Classes.on="{Binding IsAll}"
                                    AutomationProperties.Name="{Binding Name}"
                                    Command="{Binding $parent[Window].((vm:MainWindowViewModel)DataContext).AssignTagCommand}"
                                    CommandParameter="{Binding Id}">
                              <Grid ColumnDefinitions="14,4,Auto,7,*,8,Auto" Height="24">
                                <!-- Tick for all, dash for some, nothing for none —
                                     one slot, three states, never two marks at once. -->
                                <PathIcon Grid.Column="0" Data="{StaticResource RmIconCheck}"
                                          Width="9" Height="9" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                          Foreground="{DynamicResource RmAccentTextBrush}"
                                          IsVisible="{Binding IsAll}" />
                                <PathIcon Grid.Column="0" Data="{StaticResource RmIconMinus}"
                                          Width="9" Height="9" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                          Foreground="{DynamicResource RmTextSecondaryBrush}"
                                          IsVisible="{Binding IsSome}" />
                                <Border Grid.Column="2" Width="8" Height="8" CornerRadius="2"
                                        VerticalAlignment="Center" Classes="paletted"
                                        Classes.p0="{Binding IsPalette0}" Classes.p1="{Binding IsPalette1}"
                                        Classes.p2="{Binding IsPalette2}" Classes.p3="{Binding IsPalette3}"
                                        Classes.p4="{Binding IsPalette4}" Classes.p5="{Binding IsPalette5}" />
                                <TextBlock Grid.Column="4" Text="{Binding Name}" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                           TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis" />
                                <!-- "1 of 3": the dash as a number rather than a mood. -->
                                <TextBlock Grid.Column="6" Text="{Binding CountText}" Classes="mono ter"
                                           VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                              </Grid>
                            </Button>
                          </DataTemplate>
                        </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                      </ItemsControl>
                    </ScrollViewer>

                    <Border Height="1" Margin="0,4" Classes="divider" />

                    <!--
                      O22 · the create box is GONE, owner's call: tags are made in
                      Settings and only assigned here. The footer is the filter
                      flyout's two-button grammar — navigate left, act right.

                      The right-hand verb is "Remove all tags", NOT "Clear". Every
                      visible "Clear" in this app resets a FILTER, and this flyout is a
                      deliberate mirror of the one whose footer carries that word in
                      this exact slot; putting an unrecoverable data deletion there
                      under the same label would be a trap. It routes through the
                      destructive confirm (2i-6) because nothing else can bring the
                      tags back — metadata is not in the undo history, and Ctrl+Z after
                      one would repaint the pills from the already-cleared file.
                    -->
                    <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*,Auto" Margin="6,2">
                      <Button Grid.Column="0" Classes="quiet" Content="Manage tags…"
                              Command="{Binding $parent[Window].((vm:MainWindowViewModel)DataContext).ManageTagsCommand}"
                              ToolTip.Tip="Create, rename, recolour and delete tags in Settings" />
                      <Button Grid.Column="2" Classes="quiet" Content="Remove all tags"
                              Command="{Binding $parent[Window].((vm:MainWindowViewModel)DataContext).RemoveAllTagsCommand}"
                              ToolTip.ShowOnDisabled="True"
                              ToolTip.Tip="{Binding $parent[Window].((vm:MainWindowViewModel)DataContext).RemoveAllTagsTip}" />
                    </Grid>
                  </StackPanel>
                </Flyout>
              </Button.Flyout>
            </Button>
          </WrapPanel>
        </StackPanel>

        <!-- 5 · facts grid. Label column 78px so the values line up as a column of
             their own rather than ragged after variable-length labels. -->
        <Grid Margin="10,10,10,0" ColumnDefinitions="78,*" RowDefinitions="Auto,Auto,Auto,Auto,Auto,Auto">
          <TextBlock Grid.Row="0" Grid.Column="0" Text="Author" Classes="small ter" />
          <TextBlock Grid.Row="0" Grid.Column="1" Text="{Binding Authors}" Classes="small sec"
                     TextWrapping="Wrap" />

          <TextBlock Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="0" Text="Version" Classes="small ter" Margin="0,5,0,0" />
          <TextBlock Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="1" Text="{Binding Version}" Classes="small sec"
                     Margin="0,5,0,0" />

          <TextBlock Grid.Row="2" Grid.Column="0" Text="Supports" Classes="small ter" Margin="0,5,0,0" />
          <TextBlock Grid.Row="2" Grid.Column="1" Text="{Binding SupportedVersions}"
                     Classes="small sec" Margin="0,5,0,0" TextWrapping="Wrap" />

          <TextBlock Grid.Row="3" Grid.Column="0" Text="Content" Classes="small ter" Margin="0,5,0,0" />
          <TextBlock Grid.Row="3" Grid.Column="1" Text="{Binding Flags}" Classes="small sec"
                     Margin="0,5,0,0" TextWrapping="Wrap" />

          <TextBlock Grid.Row="4" Grid.Column="0" Text="Load order" Classes="small ter" Margin="0,5,0,0" />
          <TextBlock Grid.Row="4" Grid.Column="1" Text="{Binding LoadOrderText}" Classes="small sec"
                     Margin="0,5,0,0" />

          <!-- O3 · size on disk. Filled in after a background walk of the mod folder,
               so it reads "—" for the moment between selecting a row and the walk
               landing. Deliberately not part of the scan: see FolderSize. -->
          <TextBlock Grid.Row="5" Grid.Column="0" Text="Size" Classes="small ter" Margin="0,5,0,0" />
          <TextBlock Grid.Row="5" Grid.Column="1" Text="{Binding SizeText}" Classes="small sec"
                     Margin="0,5,0,0" />
        </Grid>

        <!-- 6 · dependencies. The INDEX is the point: knowing a dependency exists is
             half the answer; knowing it loads at #4 while this mod loads at #118 is
             what says the order is right. -->
        <StackPanel Margin="10,12,10,0" IsVisible="{Binding HasDependencies}">
          <TextBlock Text="DEPENDENCIES" Classes="micro" Margin="0,0,0,4" />
          <ItemsControl ItemsSource="{Binding Dependencies}">
            <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
              <DataTemplate x:DataType="vm:DependencyRowViewModel">
                <Grid ColumnDefinitions="11,6,*,Auto" Margin="0,1">
                  <PathIcon Grid.Column="0" Data="{StaticResource RmIconCheck}" Width="9" Height="9"
                            Foreground="{DynamicResource RmSuccessBrush}"
                            IsVisible="{Binding IsSatisfied}" />
                  <PathIcon Grid.Column="0" Data="{StaticResource RmIconClose}" Width="9" Height="9"
                            Foreground="{DynamicResource RmDangerBrush}"
                            IsVisible="{Binding IsMissing}" />
                  <TextBlock Grid.Column="2" Text="{Binding Name}" Classes="small sec"
                             TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                  <TextBlock Grid.Column="3" Text="{Binding PositionText}" Classes="mono ter"
                             VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                </Grid>
              </DataTemplate>
            </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
          </ItemsControl>
        </StackPanel>

        <!--
          6b · warnings (N2 · UI-5). Placed HERE, next to dependencies, rather than at
          the very bottom as the backlog put it: the two are the same species of
          content — what is wrong and what is needed — both are conditional, and
          burying the most actionable thing in the pane under four lines of Workshop
          description is the opposite of what this section is for. Notes → description
          → actions stay the stable tail either way.

          It reads the ROW's warnings rather than re-deriving them, so the pane, the
          row's tooltip and the dock cannot disagree about what is wrong with a mod.
        -->
        <StackPanel Margin="10,12,10,0"
                    IsVisible="{Binding $parent[Window].((vm:MainWindowViewModel)DataContext).SelectedModHasWarnings}">
          <TextBlock Classes="micro" Margin="0,0,0,4"
                     Text="{Binding $parent[Window].((vm:MainWindowViewModel)DataContext).SelectedModWarningHeading}" />
          <ItemsControl ItemsSource="{Binding $parent[Window].((vm:MainWindowViewModel)DataContext).SelectedModWarnings}">
            <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
              <DataTemplate x:DataType="vm:RowWarning">
                <!-- Grid, not a horizontal StackPanel: a StackPanel measures its
                     children at infinite width, so the wrapping message would never
                     wrap and would paint straight out of the pane.

                     The glyph comes from the warning's OWN tone, exactly as the dock's
                     rows do. It was hardcoded to the amber ⚠, so Achtung! showed the red
                     blocking mark in the list and an amber triangle in this pane for the
                     very same incompatibility — the panel disagreeing with the row about
                     how serious something is. Same three glyphs, same three brushes. -->
                <Grid ColumnDefinitions="11,6,*" Margin="0,1">
                  <Panel Grid.Column="0" VerticalAlignment="Top" Margin="0,3,0,0">
                    <PathIcon Data="{StaticResource RmIconError}" Width="9" Height="9"
                              Foreground="{DynamicResource RmDangerBrush}"
                              IsVisible="{Binding IsBlocking}" />
                    <PathIcon Data="{StaticResource RmIconWarning}" Width="9" Height="9"
                              Foreground="{DynamicResource RmWarningBrush}"
                              IsVisible="{Binding IsWarning}" />
                    <PathIcon Data="{StaticResource RmIconInfo}" Width="9" Height="9"
                              Foreground="{DynamicResource RmTextTertiaryBrush}"
                              IsVisible="{Binding IsInfo}" />
                  </Panel>
                  <TextBlock Grid.Column="2" Text="{Binding Message}" Classes="small sec"
                             TextWrapping="Wrap" />
                </Grid>
              </DataTemplate>
            </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
          </ItemsControl>
          <Button Classes="quiet" Content="Show in Warnings" Margin="0,6,0,0"
                  HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                  Command="{Binding $parent[Window].((vm:MainWindowViewModel)DataContext).RevealSelectedModWarningsCommand}" />
        </StackPanel>

        <!-- 7 · notes, ABOVE the description because they are the user's own. -->
        <StackPanel Margin="10,12,10,0">
          <TextBlock Text="NOTES" Classes="micro" Margin="0,0,0,4" />
          <!-- Saves on blur (1a §7). UpdateSourceTrigger=LostFocus is what gives
               that without a code-behind — a ResourceDictionary has none — and
               without writing to disk on every keystroke. -->
          <TextBox AutomationProperties.Name="Notes for this mod"
                 Text="{Binding Notes, Mode=TwoWay, UpdateSourceTrigger=LostFocus}"
                   AcceptsReturn="True" TextWrapping="Wrap" MinHeight="42"
                   Background="{DynamicResource RmBackgroundCanvasBrush}" />
        </StackPanel>

        <!-- 8 · description, clamped. BBCode is stripped upstream. -->
        <StackPanel Margin="10,12,10,0" IsVisible="{Binding HasDescription}">
          <TextBlock Text="DESCRIPTION" Classes="micro" Margin="0,0,0,4" />
          <TextBlock Text="{Binding Description}" Classes="small sec" TextWrapping="Wrap"
                     MaxLines="4" TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis" />
          <!-- O3 · offered only when the clamp is actually cutting something, so it
               never promises text that is already all on screen.
               O23 · a link, not a quiet button: it opens more of the text above it and
               changes nothing, which is the "go somewhere" side of T6's line. Still a
               Button, so it keeps focus, the keyboard and an automation name — see
               Button.link's note for why that is not negotiable. -->
          <Button Classes="link" Content="Read more" Margin="0,5,0,0"
                  HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                  AutomationProperties.Name="Read the full description"
                  IsVisible="{Binding DescriptionIsClamped}"
                  Command="{Binding $parent[Window].((vm:MainWindowViewModel)DataContext).OpenFullDescriptionCommand}" />
        </StackPanel>

        <!-- 9 · actions, as 22px quiet buttons. The "About.xml" button is GONE (T6):
             its reason promised "the XML viewer (R5)", R5 shipped without one, and a
             disabled control whose reason names a schedule goes stale the day the
             schedule moves. Open folder reaches the same file. -->
        <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="6" Margin="10,12,10,12">
          <Button Classes="quiet" Content="Open folder" Command="{Binding OpenFolderCommand}" />
          <!-- Hidden rather than disabled for a local mod: there is no Workshop page
               to open, and a permanently dead button teaches nothing. -->
          <Button Classes="quiet" Command="{Binding OpenWorkshopCommand}"
                  IsVisible="{Binding HasWorkshopUrl}">
            <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="4">
              <TextBlock Text="Workshop" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
              <PathIcon Data="{StaticResource RmIconExternal}" Width="9" Height="9"
                        VerticalAlignment="Center" />
            </StackPanel>
          </Button>
        </StackPanel>
      </StackPanel>
    </ScrollViewer>
  </DataTemplate>
</ResourceDictionary>
